  - test/math/x_frem64.lin, test/math/x_frem32.lin — compile-only lowering of frem64/frem32. PASS.
  - test/runtime/rt_rand_srand.lin — runtime srand(42)+rand, checks result is non-negative i32, prints single value. PASS.
- `while` loops: runtime execution is NOT functional (loop body never runs post-lowering). Added compile-only coverage:
  - test/runtime/rt_while_loop.lin — `while` lowering, compiles. PASS.
  - test/runtime/rt_nested_while.lin — nested `while` lowering, compiles. PASS.
  - Note: fib_loop.lin / test_while_soundness.lin have no output-check so they do NOT validate runtime loop behavior.
## Self-recursion: root-cause analysis (deep investigation, Aug 2026)

user goal: make recursion (comprehensive.lin fib, exec_control_flow.lin) actually work, not crash.
full suite on be4dad0 = 311/314 (only those 2 segfault + test_cli_wasm intended-fail).

### Two independent layers are both required, and together they are the blocker:

- **Layer 1 (lowering) — self is never captured.** `lowerFuncDeclExpr` (src/Lowering.c ~1232)
  computes free vars of the body (findFreeVars ~394) which ALWAYS includes the function's own name
  (self-call callee is not bound/control). But the closure's capture bundle is built (~1486-1510) by
  env_fetch from the OUTER env, where the self name is absent at definition time -> replaced with ERA
  (1488-1495); the closure pair is created AFTER packing (1512-1525); the self name is only bound to
  the outer env afterwards (env_add 1527-1528). Net: a recursive body's self-reference resolves to ERA.
  Consequence: `(fib n-1)` fires a `call` whose callee is era -> no dispatch rule -> the recursive call
  NEVER materializes a value -> the Bug3 p2NotMaterialized retry (checkDep) re-pushes forever.
  Measured: d(0) base case works (exit 0, prints 0); d(1) TIMES OUT (infinite spin, exit 124);
  fib(2+)/fib(5) accumulate garbage nodes -> OOB segfault (`mov (%rcx,%rax,8)` rax=0x1e847fd00000004).

- **Layer 2 (reducer) — cyclic closure duplication.** I implemented layer 1 by creating the closure
  pair BEFORE packing the bundle and, when a captured free var is the function's own name, binding it
  to the closure's own principal P0 (self-reference -> genuine graph cycle closure.P0 -> bundle ->
  self slot -> closure.P0). Result: EVEN BASE CASES (fib(0)/fib(1), d(0)) segfault. Merely capturing
  the cyclic env makes the eager interaction-net reducer try to DUPLICATE the cyclic structure when the
  closure is copied (e.g. either/dup of the closure ref), which does not terminate -> unbounded net
  growth -> OOB. The reducer has no lazy-sharing/cycle-aware duplication.

### Conclusion
Correct self-recursion needs BOTH the lowering self-capture fix AND a reducer able to duplicate cyclic
(recursive) closure environments without unbounded growth — i.e. sharing-based / cycle-aware duplication
semantics in the interaction-net reducer. That is a research-scale change to Pass_PicReduceToRuntime/
Pass_PicReduceLowering with high regression risk to the now-perfect 38/38 runtime suite. Not delivered;
tree reverted to stable be4dad0 (311/314). Empirically confirmed: enabling self-capture alone (layer 1)
crashes even non-recursive base cases because of layer 2.
